{
  "dom_id": "step-q124174",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273134/assets/d7a164e749bbaaaf1841c04dde663805db000976947086912e37694f76c5aa85.png)\n\nConsider the segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, and the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=-3u+2v+1,\\,y=-u-v.\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ under the action of $T$ is the segment $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}$ in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following diagrams shows $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}?$",
  "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3u+2v+1 \\\\ -u-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3u+2v \\\\ -u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(11,0)$ and $(-8,2).$\n\nDrawing this segment in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273134/assets/ed58ba894f37c39d56c32a20425b928b4b22e130449e02396cdf01d95b66c27c.png)",
